    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502-a1">

                <pb facs="0598" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg578"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 63.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the
                            United States in Japan</hi>, <placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Kanagawa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1864-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 17,
                        1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A convention has been agreed on, ready for
                    signature, between the Tycoon and the United States, Great Britain, France, and
                    the Netherlands, by which three millions (3,000,000) of dollars are to be paid
                    for indemnities and expenses occasioned by outrages of Choshu, to be divided as
                    the said powers shall agree, or at their option a new port will be opened in the
                    Inland sea.</p>
                <p>My colleagues desire the above communicated to the ministers of their governments
                    in Washington.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident in
                            Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
